+# Emilyfn 0.1.0 provenance
+
+Emilyfn's C#/WPF interface, process manager, diagnostics and synthetic tests are new source in this directory. License: GPL-3.0, included in `LICENSE`.
+
+The local launch protocol and static compatibility arguments were adapted from Reboot Launcher at:
+
+- https://github.com/Auties00/Reboot-Launcher/tree/c6f82298b167ef2076bb59dc621f13dc5bd8d390
+- `common/lib/src/game/game_metadata.dart` and game constants at that revision; GPL-3.0.
+
+The `-fltoken` and `-caldera` entries in `compatibility-args.json` are exact public literals from `game_metadata.dart` at that pinned commit (lines 221–222), verified through GitHub before publication. They were not read from the user's accounts, machine, environment, or login session. The public Caldera payload records a generation date of 2021-12-05. Their argument-string SHA-256 values are `0bf0d8e7c07fcbca6a5ce666fccb70c216207d31750c80fdacc3e8e70057e85d` and `a9bf563cee35441cfba6be72f6c05c0bae038deef08951a0d23ad208e2b1fee8` respectively. Runtime local-profile names/passwords are generated separately and diagnostic exports redact these argument fields.
+
+Bundled components:
+
+| Component | Fixed source/build |
+| --- | --- |
+| Seasons 19–30 Auth, Client and Server DLLs | https://github.com/EmilyUwU666/reboot-2711/actions/runs/34847063986 — workflow commit `4aab950a0d518b0b13e5c545f49a0568d27341f8` |
+| Corresponding DLL/authentication source | `Reboot-S19-S30-Candidate1-Source`, artifact `10348805925` from that run |
+| Local backend and Windows Node runtime | https://github.com/EmilyUwU666/reboot-2711/actions/runs/34817850310 — workflow commit `dc15344b6d9c0b0c9e8e0f946931a04227550813` |
+| Backend upstream | https://github.com/Lawin0129/LawinServer/tree/7f0f26d7a772c6122c42b1783fd75f497e86d3a9 |
+| Node runtime | Official Windows x64 Node 24.21.0, with original license and build provenance in `resources/backend` |
+| Desktop runtime | Microsoft .NET 10 Windows Desktop, self-contained publish; exact patch recorded in package build metadata |
+
+Required component SHA-256 values are enforced by `build.ps1`:
+
+```
+032ea3458f0a84fceeb158d20d03e7b97511e05004fd0087051421c43d9bced1  Reboot-S19-S30-Server.dll
+246b36a8a49fa7681ae039d8bf9424edd63b82194f9a90e42ecd005a1d0c1dfa  Reboot-S19-S30-Client.dll
+878c3d6141e2ca9bf0b140f02f38d59393dbf15b6b954ab387c31387eac70ce3  Reboot-S19-S30-Auth.dll
+```
+
+The interface artwork is original vector geometry embedded in XAML. The icon is generated by `build-icon.ps1`. No Fortnite artwork or game assets are bundled.
+
+Upstream notices and licenses remain with the bundled components. The .NET notices are available at https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/blob/main/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.TXT and https://github.com/dotnet/wpf/blob/main/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt .
diff --git a/launcher/README.md b/launcher/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..c6c0a44
--- /dev/null
+++ b/launcher/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,57 @@
+# Emilyfn
+
+A portable Windows x64 launcher made for Emily's local Fortnite setup.
+
+## Start playing
+
+1. Download **Emilyfn-Windows-x64** from the successful Emilyfn build's Artifacts section.
+2. Extract the **whole ZIP** into a folder, such as `C:\Games\Emilyfn`. Keep `Emilyfn.exe`, `compatibility-args.json`, and `resources` together.
+3. Open `Emilyfn.exe`.
+4. Open **Library → Browse** and select the Fortnite folder containing `FortniteGame` and `Engine`.
+5. Check the release number (for example, `27.11`) and select **Add to library**.
+6. Go to **Play** and select **Play Fortnite**. With the default settings, Emilyfn starts the backend and host before opening the client.
+7. When the client reaches the lobby, ready up. **Copy join command** also provides `open 127.0.0.1:7777` for the in-game console.
+
+The backend, Node runtime, .NET runtime, authentication DLL, server DLL and client DLL are included. There is no separate DLL picker or runtime installation. Fortnite game files are not included.
+
+## Controls
+
+- **Start host** starts just the host and backend. The default host runs without rendering a window.
+- **Stop client**, **Stop host**, and **Stop all** control instances Emilyfn started. An existing external backend and unrelated programs are left running.
+- **Settings** saves your local display name and automatic/headless host preferences.
+- **Logs → Export diagnostic ZIP** collects launcher, game, backend and DLL startup diagnostics, with common credential fields redacted.
+- Closing Emilyfn stops its game instances and its own backend. Keep it open while playing.
+
+Build selection is saved, and the host and client must use the same selected installation and release. Emilyfn reads `Fortnite+Release-27.11` separately from an engine version such as `5.4.0`.
+
+## If a session fails
+
+Read the last stage in **Logs** and export a diagnostic ZIP. Authentication, login, module initialization and host listening have time limits. A process that exits is reported with its exit code.
+
+The backend uses loopback ports 3551, 80 and 8080. The host uses UDP 7777. If a port is occupied by an incompatible program, Emilyfn reports the problem; it does not stop that program or change Windows services.
+
+**Listening** means the launched host owns UDP port 7777. **Client active** means login and client SDK initialization completed. These states do not prove that a match loaded successfully. A client stuck at Connecting can still require a server/DLL fix.
+
+## Compatibility
+
+This release bundles the existing **experimental Seasons 19–30 candidate 1** components. The launcher accepts installed releases from 19.xx through 30.xx; this does not certify every patch for complete gameplay. The earlier 27.11 host crash/client Connecting issue has not been confirmed resolved by a live Fortnite test.
+
+This is a local private-session launcher. It does not join Epic's live matchmaking, download Fortnite, or ask for a real Epic password. Use the game files you already have. Windows x64 is required.
+
+## Data
+
+Settings and logs: `%LOCALAPPDATA%\Emilyfn`.
+
+The bundled backend is copied into `%LOCALAPPDATA%\Emilyfn\backend-candidate1` on first use, and that copy is reused so local backend data is retained. The package's original resources remain unchanged.
+
+## Build from source
+
+Use Windows x64, the .NET 10 SDK, PowerShell, and the full source artifact. To rebuild the launcher with components from an extracted portable package:
+
+```powershell
+.\launcher\build.ps1 -DllDirectory C:\Games\Emilyfn\resources\dlls -BackendDirectory C:\Games\Emilyfn\resources\backend -OutputDirectory .\Emilyfn-build
+```
+
+The script generates the icon and publishes a self-contained WPF executable. The workflow also builds small native test fixtures with the Visual C++ x64 toolchain and runs `Emilyfn.Tests`. Those fixtures test launcher mechanics; they contain no Fortnite code and are not included in the portable package.
+
+`PROVENANCE.md` identifies component source and build runs. `BUILD-INFO.txt` in the portable package records the actual compiler/runtime and artifact hashes. The source artifact includes the launcher source and the corresponding existing component source archive. See `LICENSE` and component licenses for redistribution terms.
diff --git a/launcher/build.ps1 b/launcher/build.ps1
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..0655e97
--- /dev/null
+++ b/launcher/build.ps1
@@ -0,0 +1,46 @@
+param(
+    [Parameter(Mandatory=$true)][string]$DllDirectory,
+    [Parameter(Mandatory=$true)][string]$BackendDirectory,
+    [string]$OutputDirectory = "$PSScriptRoot/../Emilyfn-dist"
+)
+$ErrorActionPreference = 'Stop'
+$dllRoot = (Resolve-Path $DllDirectory).Path
+$backendRoot = (Resolve-Path $BackendDirectory).Path
+$out = [System.IO.Path]::GetFullPath($OutputDirectory)
+if (Test-Path $out) { throw 'Use a new output directory so existing files cannot enter the package.' }
+$expected = @{
+    'Reboot-S19-S30-Server.dll' = '032ea3458f0a84fceeb158d20d03e7b97511e05004fd0087051421c43d9bced1'
+    'Reboot-S19-S30-Client.dll' = '246b36a8a49fa7681ae039d8bf9424edd63b82194f9a90e42ecd005a1d0c1dfa'
+    'Reboot-S19-S30-Auth.dll' = '878c3d6141e2ca9bf0b140f02f38d59393dbf15b6b954ab387c31387eac70ce3'
+}
+foreach ($name in $expected.Keys) {
+    if ((Get-FileHash (Join-Path $dllRoot $name) -Algorithm SHA256).Hash -ne $expected[$name]) { throw "Unexpected DLL: $name" }
+}
+$backendInfo = Get-Content (Join-Path $backendRoot 'BUILD-INFO.txt') -Raw
+$nodeMatch = [regex]::Match($backendInfo, 'Node runtime SHA256: ([a-fA-F0-9]{64})')
+if (!$nodeMatch.Success) { throw 'The backend runtime provenance is missing.' }
+if ((Get-FileHash (Join-Path $backendRoot 'runtime/node.exe') -Algorithm SHA256).Hash -ne $nodeMatch.Groups[1].Value) { throw 'The backend Node runtime hash differs.' }
+& "$PSScriptRoot/build-icon.ps1"
+dotnet publish "$PSScriptRoot/Emilyfn.App/Emilyfn.App.csproj" -c Release -r win-x64 --self-contained true -o $out
+if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { throw 'Emilyfn publish failed.' }
+$null = New-Item -ItemType Directory -Path "$out/resources"
+Copy-Item $dllRoot "$out/resources/dlls" -Recurse
+Copy-Item $backendRoot "$out/resources/backend" -Recurse
+foreach ($name in @('compatibility-args.json', 'README.md', 'PROVENANCE.md', 'LICENSE')) { Copy-Item "$PSScriptRoot/$name" $out }
+$sdk = dotnet --version
+$runtime = (Get-Content "$PSScriptRoot/Emilyfn.App/obj/project.assets.json" -Raw | ConvertFrom-Json).libraries.PSObject.Properties.Name | Where-Object { $_ -match 'Microsoft\.(NETCore|WindowsDesktop)\.App\.Runtime\.win-x64/' }
+@"
+Emilyfn 0.1.0 - Windows x64
+SDK: $sdk
+Published runtimes: $($runtime -join ', ')
+Workflow commit: $env:GITHUB_SHA
+Workflow run: https://github.com/$env:GITHUB_REPOSITORY/actions/runs/$env:GITHUB_RUN_ID
+Components: Seasons 19-30 candidate 1 DLLs and portable backend candidate 1.
+Runtime limits: experimental game support; complete Fortnite matches not verified.
+"@ | Set-Content "$out/BUILD-INFO.txt" -Encoding utf8
+$hashes = Get-ChildItem $out -Recurse -File | Sort-Object FullName | ForEach-Object {
+    $relative = [System.IO.Path]::GetRelativePath($out, $_.FullName).Replace('\', '/')
+    "$((Get-FileHash $_.FullName -Algorithm SHA256).Hash.ToLowerInvariant())  $relative"
+}
+$hashes | Set-Content "$out/SHA256SUMS.txt" -Encoding utf8
+Write-Host "Emilyfn portable package created at $out"
